# Known replay gaps -- scripts/test-migrations.sh
# ============================================================================
# Migrations listed here are ALLOWED to fail during a from-scratch replay.
# Every one fails for the same structural reason, established by replaying the
# full history into a scratch PostgreSQL 14 database on 2026-07-25:
#
#   Some of this project's schema was never created by a committed migration.
#   Two drizzle migrations are referenced by db/migrations/meta/_journal.json
#   but their SQL files are absent from the repo entirely --
#   0002_steady_darwin.sql and 0003_thin_hairball.sql. Their snapshots survive
#   (meta/0002_snapshot.json, meta/0003_snapshot.json) but the DDL does not.
#   Other objects were created directly through the Supabase dashboard and were
#   never captured as migrations at all.
#
#   So the objects below exist in production and in db/schema/*.ts, but nothing
#   in supabase/migrations/ or db/migrations/ creates them, and any migration
#   that references one cannot replay from scratch:
#
#     character_equipment, campaign_characters, starter_character_templates,
#     ai_usage, the chunk_type enum, characters.class_levels,
#     characters.skill_proficiencies
#
# This file is a record of that debt, not an excuse for it. Its purpose is to
# let the replay test be enforcing TODAY for everything that is not already
# broken: a migration NOT listed here that fails to replay fails CI.
#
# ============================================================================
# RULES
# ============================================================================
# * NEVER add a newly written migration to this file. If a migration you are
#   adding cannot replay, the migration is wrong, or it depends on an object
#   that also needs a migration -- write that one too.
# * Entries may only be REMOVED. When the missing DDL above is finally
#   backfilled as a real migration, delete the entries it unblocks. The test
#   reports any listed migration that has started passing.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line, '#' starts a comment.
# ============================================================================

